@startuml
title Wait and approval suspension lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Suspended run" as Suspended #FFF0D9 {
  state "Signal wait\nwait:{token}:{node}" as SignalWait #FFF0D9
  state "Event wait\nwait:{token}:{node}" as EventWait #FFF0D9
  state "Timer wait\nwait:{token}:{node}" as TimerWait #FFF0D9
  state "Retry wait\nretry:{token}:{attempt}" as RetryWait #FFE0C8
  state "Durable-yield wait\nyield:{token}:{transition}" as YieldWait #F8DADA
  state "Approval\napproval:{token}:{node}" as Approval #FFE0C8 {
    state "Collecting decisions" as Collecting #FFE0C8
    [*] --> Collecting
    Collecting --> Collecting : approve [<latex>|D| < q</latex>]\n/ record unique decisionId,\nemit approvalRecorded
  }
}

state "Resumed in Route phase\n(disposition completed)" as ResumedCompleted #D9EFDF
state "Resumed in Route phase\n(disposition rejected)" as ResumedRejected #E7DCF5
state "Re-entered in Enter phase\n(node re-executes, attempt + 1)" as ReEntered #E9F5EA
state "Cancelled\n(compensation unwinds)" as Cancelled #E7DCF5

SignalWait --> ResumedCompleted : signal [name matches]\n/ payload replaces value
EventWait --> ResumedCompleted : event [name matches]\n/ payload replaces value
TimerWait --> ResumedCompleted : timerFired\n[<latex>d = d_{\mathrm{expected}} \;\land\; \mathrm{now} \ge d</latex>]
Collecting --> ResumedCompleted : approve [<latex>|D| \ge q</latex>]\n/ waitSatisfied, approvalRecorded, runResumed
Collecting --> ResumedRejected : reject [actor is an approver]\n/ disposition rejected
RetryWait --> ReEntered : timerFired [exact deadline]\nor retry command
Suspended --> Cancelled : cancel command (run level)

note right of YieldWait #FDECEA
Current behavior: no command class accepts a
durable-yield suspension, so this wait has no
resume transition. Only run-level cancel or
migrate can act on the run. Tracked as a known
gap in the roadmap.
end note
note bottom of Approval #FFF3C9
An empty approver set admits any ledger-authorized
actor. Each actor decides at most once and every
decisionId is globally unique. The approval deadline
(from the node timeout policy) is recorded and
published as the run's due_at but is not auto-enforced:
no timedOut disposition fires, and the recovery scan
reports an error until the approval resolves.
end note
note left of TimerWait #EAF7EE
An unparseable deadline expression yields a wait
with no due_at; timerFired then fails with
"timer has no deadline". Validate computed
deadlines before deploying.
end note
@enduml
